    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d24-a4">

                <pb facs="0093" n="43" xml:id="pg43"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 93.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gelletich to Mr. Tripp.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">U.
                                S. Consular Agency</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Fiume</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1894-03-23"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 23,
                    1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to inform you that the chief of the
                    political district of Sussak-Tersato appeared in my office and informed me that
                    John Benich is canceled from the rolls of the army, and further informed me that
                    he is instructed to give satisfaction for the offense to U. S. consular
                    authority, and requested me in what manner I require such satisfaction.</p>
                <p>I beg you to inform me what I am to do, and what kind of satisfaction I am to ask
                    of the said chief of political district.</p>
                <p>Awaiting your kind reply,</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Giov. Gelletich.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
